        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "641c884a-9cc0-5775-b94c-b0adcf85d7fe",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: The Honourable The Irish Society, livery companies of the City of London\n- Events: Plantation of Ulster\n- Places: County Londonderry, Ulster, Ireland, Great Britain, Armagh, Cavan, Fermanagh, Tyrone, Tyrconnell, Londonderry\n- People: King James I\n\nFacts:\n- In 1613, The Honourable The Irish Society was set up as a consortium of livery companies of the City of London to colonise County Londonderry during the Plantation of Ulster.\n- The Plantation of Ulster was the organised colonisation of the province of Ulster in Ireland by people from Great Britain during the reign of King James I.\n- The official Plantation of Ulster comprised an estimated half a million acres of arable land in the counties of Armagh, Cavan, Fermanagh, Tyrone, Tyrconnell, and Londonderry.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
